<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama, History</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> i plan to use alot of interview style dialouges since the foundation primarily documents the entity through the locals who tell its story, but it wont be the primary format.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
•A Mountain range is actually the site of a massive battle between giant stone entities<br />
•A local tribe allied with one side of the conflict and fought with them in the war using what they called &quot;magic&quot;, which was just reality bending to a much lesser level than an actual reality bender.<br />
•During the war the chief of the allied mountains was wounded, the other entities fought to the death to defend it.<br />
•the tribes had to sacrifice their &quot;magic&quot; to save it. leaving them vulnerable to european invasion later on.<br />
•The mountain has now healed enough to become active and the foundation has to befriend the tribe to learn how to contain it<br />
•The foundation becomes uneasy as the tribe further uses their leverage to make policitcal gains.<br />
•The tribe ultimatley use more leverage, proposing regaining their reality bending abilities.<br />
•Once an agreement is made, the tribe helps contain the entity<br />
•The foundation learns to contain the entity. but then learn that the siksika t<br />
were not the only tribe to have saved one of these entities.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> chief mountain is a siksika story of a giant chief who laid down and became a mountain. this is a story told to outsiders the real story is that the mountain was a chief of a band of giant stone humanoids and was nearly killed in battle. The surrounding mountain range is a graveyard of the battle in which the massive entities dead remain. the local tribe are &quot;keepers&quot; of the mountain and tasked with keeping it alive, as they were allies in the battle and had to sacrifice their reality bending abilities to keep it alive. The mountain has finally healed enough to awaken, and they soon learn that other tribes have done the same. Numerous infact, threatening to ignite another massive war of the stone giants. Something that would be extremely hard to contain, let alone keep secret.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> a modern twist on a traditional story to help preserve one of my tribe's stories, and to bring more real indigenous stories/cryptids other than the well known bigfoot or wendigo</p>
<p>**Additional Notes:*</p>

