<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi Red Dissent, let's take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>So first off, you've got the components of the pitch swapped. Your elevator pitch should be a summary of the base anomalous properties of the scp, and your central narrative should be the part where you go into a bit more detail. Do edit this for future reviewers.</p>
<p>Even then, I do have a few clarifying questions about the narrative, as I'm not entirely sure I understand what happens:</p>
<p>Ok, so long ago, the mountains were actually giants? Then the tribes were reality-benders? They fought a war, okay&#8230; but how does the reality-bending tie into the giant mythos? I know you said they had to sacrifice their powers, but why?</p>
<p>Fast forward to the present, I don't get the whole &quot;political gains&quot; angle. Isn't the mountain already being contained by the tribes' sacrifice? What's the Foundation's role in this now?</p>
<p>Basically, there are a ton of moving parts atm and I'm not sure how they connect. Feel free to elaborate further in another post below. If you decide to do so, please drop me another PM and I'll take a second look. All the best!</p>

